## Step 4 — `__main__.py`

Plain Python CLI. No LangGraph.

### Args
```
--episode-id <id>          Enrich one episode
--season <slug> <n>        Enrich all episodes in a season
--all <slug>               Enrich all scraped episodes for a series
--show-text                Print the formatted input text and exit (no model call)
--skip-existing            Skip episodes where mood_enriched.json already exists
```

### Series registry
```python
from backend.scraping.series_config import THE_OFFICE, SeriesConfig

SERIES_REGISTRY: dict[str, SeriesConfig] = {
    "the_office": THE_OFFICE,
}
```

### Episode discovery
For `--season` and `--all`: list `data/raw/` directories matching `{series_slug}_s{nn}_e{nn}`. Do NOT re-run scraper discovery — read from disk. Pattern:
```python
import re
pattern = re.compile(rf"^{re.escape(series_slug)}_s\d{{2}}_e\d{{2}}$")
episode_ids = sorted(d for d in os.listdir(data_root) if pattern.match(d))
```
For `--season`: also filter by `_s{n:02d}_`.

### Model loading
Load the classifier once before the episode loop, not inside the loop:
```python
from transformers import pipeline as hf_pipeline
classifier = hf_pipeline("zero-shot-classification", model=MODEL_ID)
```

### Progress
Print to stderr: `enriching the_office_s02_e04 ...` per episode. Print summary at end: `Done: X enriched, Y skipped, Z failed`.

### `--show-text` mode
Load `extracted_data.json`, call `format_for_zero_shot`, print to stdout, exit. No model loaded.

